 "text": "Hi, how's your day been so far? In Italian, it's per day with an additional n for each full day the treatment lasts. You can say bisogna tavola per die for one day, or bisogna tavola per due for two full days. That would be bisogna tassello per due if you show up and it' free, or bisogna cod per due if you pay for it. You've got the basics down. Remember to smile and say please. Say please again after each one, and stop after ten. It' a bit like playing the musical chairs game as a child. You' got the basics down. Remember to smile and say please.",
